Elasticsearch and OpenSearch type mappings for the data models are now generated from the models (:func:`peat.es_mappings.model_mapping` and :func:`peat.es_mappings.peat_index_mappings`) instead of being maintained by hand, using the type annotations and the ``elastic_type`` field overrides (`#51 <https://github.com/sandialabs/PEAT/issues/51>`__). This adds mappings for ``host.files``, ``host.successful_pulls``, and the ``host.mac_vendor``, ``host.label``, ``host.comment`` and ``host.serial_number`` fields in the non-host indices, adds a ``.text`` subfield to ``event.action``, and changes ``event.severity`` from ``long`` to ``keyword`` (except in the log index), since device event severities are strings such as ``debug``.
